ble terrain. While\nconfidence in location and rainfall rates remain low at this time,\nthe potential for rapidly rising rivers, streams, normally dry\narroyos and slot canyons are possible Sunday through Monday.\n\nPlease follow the evolving forecast, especially if your plans\nincluding recreating or commuting across eastern Utah and western\nColorado Sunday onward. Also, keep in mind weather potential above\nyour location and upstream, particularly for those who reside below\nsensitive terrain like recent burn scars.","ends":"2026-10-12T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Delta, CO; Dolores, CO; Garfield, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Mesa, CO; Moffat, CO; Montezuma, CO; Montrose, CO; Ouray, CO; Rio Blanco, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Daggett, UT; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT; Uintah, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-12T05:55:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 120555 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1155 PM MDT Sun Oct 11 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - An additional 1-2\" of precipitation is expected over the high terrain through Wednesday, with locally higher amounts likely over the Uintas. Some of this will be in the form of snow down to 9000 feet...but most significant above 10000 feet. - Winds will b","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-11T18:53:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Gusty winds up to 40-50 mph continue through the overnight hours, with showers and storms decreasing in intensity this evening. Wet weather remains in the forecast through at least mid week, with snow chances increasing over the higher terrain as the week progresses. Critical fire weather conditions are not anticipa